# These four were inherited from the monorepo root this project used to live
# under, and stopped applying the moment it became its own repository. Nothing
# announced that: `git status` simply started offering to commit schematic.pdf.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
.venv/
# Not ours to redistribute. schematic.pdf is the Forgix board's, and
# docs/article/ holds a publisher's author guidelines. Both stay local; the
# README says where schematic.pdf comes from.
*.pdf

# Build outputs
firmware/build*/
rtl/build/

# M4: the COCO corpus, the teacher embedding cache, and training runs. All
# regenerable from model/*.py, and together tens of gigabytes.
model/data/
model/cache/

# ...with one exception: the shipped export. 994 KB of weights.bin, testvec.bin
# and export.json, and eleven defaults across firmware/CMakeLists.txt,
# rtl/Makefile, host/demo.py, host/cam.py, the four firmware/test_*.c harnesses
# and tools/probe_prompts.py all point at this exact path. Without it in the
# tree a fresh clone cannot build forgix_m5 or run the demo at all, which is a
# strange thing for the repository of a working appliance.
#
# git will not re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so every
# level has to be excluded and re-admitted in turn. That is why one directory
# costs four lines, and why the run name appears here: it is the same name
# export.json carries and the board prints a crc32 for.
model/runs/*
!model/runs/so400m-full-a05/
model/runs/so400m-full-a05/*
!model/runs/so400m-full-a05/export/

# Efinity project scratch — regenerated on every synthesis run.
# .peri.xml is derived from the matching .isf by rtl/mk_peri.py, so the .isf is
# the source of truth and this is an artifact.
rtl/outflow/
rtl/work_pt/
rtl/work_syn/
rtl/work_pnr/
rtl/*.peri.xml
rtl/*_import_issue.csv
rtl/link_narrow.sdc
rtl/link_wide.sdc
rtl/RUNPNR_*

# `screen -L` drops this in the cwd. host/mon.py is the supported way to
# capture a firmware report; see its docstring for why DTR matters.
screenlog.*

# Third-party, not redistributed. Both come from Adiuvo's developer repo
# (bitbucket.org/adiuvo-engineering/forgix_public) and both are kept on disk
# here because you want them before you need them, not after:
#   vendor/plasm_led/        the known-good example bitstream, plus the Efinity
#                            pinout reports docs/pinmap.md cites as a source.
#                            Those reports are Efinity tool output, headed
#                            "Copyright (C) 2013 - 2025 Efinix Inc."
#   firmware/vendor/*.uf2    the Forge Loader image, docs/building.md's
#                            un-bricking path
vendor/
firmware/vendor/
